---
description: WaroTrans mandatory project rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Before modifying WaroTrans code, always read and obey `/rules`.

Priority:
1. `/rules/00-PROJECT-CONTEXT.md`
2. `/rules/01-SYSTEM-ARCHITECTURE.md`
3. `/rules/02-DOMAIN-RULES.md`
4. `/rules/03-WORKFLOW-RUNTIME-RULES.md`
5. `/rules/04-MODULE-COMMUNICATION-RULES.md`
6. `/rules/05-NAVIGATION-RULES.md`
7. `/rules/06-CODING-STANDARDS.md`
8. feature-specific rules
9. `/rules/99-AI-CURSOR-RULES.md`

Never introduce a new domain entity, DB table/collection, status, Step Type,
module dependency, or architecture pattern unless explicitly requested.

Never create TransportMovement, BindingSource, TrafficResource, or TrafficReservation
entities/tables.

If code or an older document conflicts with `/rules`, report the conflict before changing
domain behavior. Do not silently guess.

After code changes, run the relevant build/tests and report failures explicitly.
